,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.7.beta4\nGodot v4.7.rc1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta4 - macOS Tahoe (26.5.1) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Mobile) - integrated Apple M3 Max (Apple9) - Apple M3 Max (14 threads) - 36.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the Paste as Replacement option when pasting nodes with children, the whole thing goes upside-down:\n- it straight up doesn't work. the new (replaced) nodes don't appear in the tree.\n- the sprite names are now reset to something else.\n- undo doesn't undo. yikes.\n\nI can't believe this slipped through my testing... ugh. 🤦🏼\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/652dde45-6094-40bc-91b7-d986db2f679f\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nWhen Paste as Replacement is used, the object that is being replaced along with all its children, should be freed, and the object that is replacing it with all its children should take its place instead.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nPaste as Replacement an object with children.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[paste_as_replacement_mrp_2026-06-11_11-59-34.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28833679/paste_as_replacement_mrp_2026-06-11_11-59-34.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/user